 by the solar warmth generates water.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.52,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-85-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2079018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"822c85880ec4d4ad83cadeff5897214ce18289eec3c1b0e9a2a0c35a9ebdbf51","compact":"00dfd1bc0a03fdbac008d6848c7ad363d00a13b92c017255e3c5cd9d8744fc77","nasal":"00dfd1bc0a03fdbac008d6848c7ad363d00a13b92c017255e3c5cd9d8744fc77"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-79-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":79,"verse":19,"english":"And Kaikeyi's son was overpowered and drowned by the mountain of grief, having thoughts (of Rāma) for its entire crags, sighs for its mineral substance, disgust with the avocations of life, for its trees, mental feebleness through grief for its summits, stupor for the animals inhabiting it, and burning for its annual shrubs and bamboos.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-85-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2079019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c480ce5286a53b46577349c6c0021ec3d06936989851655393bb32b8c1cdbd65","compact":"9cbcbec4706d83aaf450761b4d5d80282ef4c2027e7e3dd1fd92708c9d674586","nasal":"ce3df837ea183e087c40f5efbf8fdb88941f69c549487cb5ebb668e155549b2f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-79-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":79,"verse":20,"english":"And Kaikeyi's son was overpowered and drowned by the mountain of grief, having thoughts (of Rāma) for its entire crags, sighs for its mineral substance, disgust with the avocations of life, for its trees, mental feebleness through grief for its summits, stupor for the animals inhabiting it, and burning for its annual shrubs and bamboos.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-85-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"sour